## Provenance

ps5-pandora is an **independent, from-scratch implementation**. It shares no
source code with any other project.

The project was *inspired by* the idea of a browser-served all-in-one manager
for a jailbroken PlayStation 5, an idea popularised by:

  * Prospero Manager (ProsperoMgr) — <https://github.com/notmaj0r/ProsperoMgr>
    Licensed GPL-3.0. No code was copied or adapted from this project. Credit
    for the concept and for proving it worth building belongs to its authors.

The architecture, the module boundaries, the metadata rules and every line in
this repository were written for this project. Where a behaviour was learned by
observing another implementation, the behaviour was described first and then
implemented here independently.

## Third-party components

Components linked into or bundled with a release are listed here with their
licences. This list is maintained by hand; see CONTRIBUTING.md.

  * **None.** No third-party library is linked into a build. The project uses
    the C++ standard library only: the JSON reader, the SHA-256 implementation,
    the ZIP writer and the HTTP server are all part of this repository, which is
    why there is nothing here to vendor, patch or audit on the console.

  * PS5 Payload SDK (John Törnblom and contributors) — see the SDK's own licence.
    Required to build for hardware; not vendored into this repository. It
    supplies the compiler wrapper and the `libkernel` import stubs.
